paragraph start
todo: broot step 0: rules, read first. Only managed files (my
files) get the safety net. Every other file works as in plain
broot and the plain shell: no server, no git, nothing blocked.
Managed (proposed, Shape confirms): any .aiu file, and any dir
inside the loaded notation folder. The server decides with a new
command, managed PATH, answering yes or no. If the server is not
reachable, managed means a .aiu file only.
A change to a managed path never falls back to plain file calls.
If the server is down it is refused with a clear message.
One crate, aiu-shell/aiu-files, is the only code allowed to change
files. Broot and the shell use it by path dependency. It is std
only: a small HTTP client for 127.0.0.1:8080/cmd. The build fails
if any other code changes files (step 5).
Limit: an outside tool or ^rm can still change files. The git
facts watcher of the server can report those.
Planned.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: broot step 1: list of file changing places. Read so far.
Managed file changes to replace: browser_state.rs:680
trash::delete, stage_state.rs:467 trash::delete_all, verbs.hjson
line 76 cp -r (lines 46, 105, 152, 157 are commented out), and
launchable.rs:195 plus verb/external_execution.rs which run any
external command from a verb, also from user config.
Appends to a path the user names: verb/write.rs:25,
app/selection.rs:88, verb/external_execution.rs:123.
Broot own files, allowed, never routed: conf/default.rs:32,36,
shell_install/*.rs, kitty/image_renderer.rs:498,569,
net/server.rs:33,95, preview/preview_transformer.rs:214-263.
Trash view only handles the system trash: trash/*.rs,
app/panel_state.rs. It stays for unmanaged files.
Broot has no internal verb to create, rename, copy or move a file:
only trash, delete_trashed_file, restore_trashed_file, purge_trash.
Those come from verbs.hjson as external commands.
Left: read verbs.hjson lines 36 to 80 and list resources/ in one
read, then write the final list here.
Planned.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: broot step 2: server first. Verified in AIU ECOSYSTEM/
server/main.rs: commands write, delete, move are in the table near
line 1055. file_delete and file_move refuse anything that is not
a file, call save_first before, and commit_for makes one git
commit per call, about 11 s. move creates parent dirs. write takes
text only, so a binary copy cannot be sent as text.
Add as server commands, each one commit whatever the file count:
managed PATH (yes or no), mkdir DIR, copy FROM (target on the next
line, copied inside the server), delete DIR and move DIR (refuse if
any file in it is untracked by git).
After a move or delete the answer lists broken links and layout
card targets, because a layout target may be a full path.
Read first: abs_path (what happens with a path outside the loaded
folder), save_first (the untracked rule and the approval word),
commit_for (can it commit a whole dir at once).
Planned.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: broot step 3: crate aiu-shell/aiu-files. Functions: managed,
delete, move_to, copy, mkdir, write, each taking a path. Managed
path: send the server command and return its answer as the result.
Unmanaged path: plain std call, same result type. Server down on a
managed path: refuse. Timeouts, no dependencies, one small file per
concern. Unit tests with a fake server on a local port.
Planned.
paragraph end

