paragraph start
todo: broot step 8: shell side, forced by code. Five locks. Only
my files (managed, step 0) are forced, other paths keep the plain
behaviour inside the same command. Classified from the code, inline
test code excluded.
GATE, managed paths go through aiu-files, each at the command entry
(all under aiu-shell/shell/crates): aiu-shell-command/src/filesystem
rm.rs (fn rm at 122, removal helpers 474 to 490), save.rs (opens
files 451 to 466), umkdir.rs (create_dir at 144), umv.rs (uu_mv::mv
at 251), ucp.rs (uu_cp), utouch.rs (uu_touch::touch at 268).
Redirection: aiu-shell-engine/src/eval_ir.rs fn open_file near 2389.
Polars save: arrow, avro, csv, ndjson, parquet, one call each.
EXTERNAL, lock 2: aiu-shell-command/src/system/run_external.rs
(Command::new at 175, spawn at 297 and 305) and exec.rs (75, 114).
aiu-shell-screen/src/command_runner.rs: Command::new at 88 and 194
runs the shell binary itself, so the child has the same locks. But
219 and 229 run lines with sh, and run_fullscreen at 305 runs a
line in the real terminal: gate the words of the line before they
run. foreground.rs, process/child.rs and jobs.rs are libraries
below: confirm with grep that every caller is gated.
ALLOWED, shell own state, never routed: command_runner.rs 331 and
629, engine_state.rs 783, history_import.rs 307, config_reset.rs
59 to 96, cmd-extra/build.rs, the example plugin second_custom_
value.rs.
TO READ before classifying: path.rs 980, history_.rs 100, cmd-
plugin util.rs 98 to 109, plugin-core communication_mode 205 to 288,
explore app.rs 341, command_runner.rs lines 215 to 235.
TESTS, ignore: glob_from.rs, dc_glob, repl.rs from 2054, tree.rs
from 360, interruptible_unix.rs, gstat from 479.
Workspace: aiu-shell/shell/Cargo.toml, [workspace.dependencies] at
line 93: add aiu-files = { path = "../aiu-files" }.
Lock 1, builtins: the GATE list above calls aiu-files for a managed
path. Others keep their code.
Lock 2, external programs: refuse rm, rmdir, unlink, mv, cp, mkdir,
touch, ln, dd, tee, truncate, shred, install, rsync, chmod, chown
when any argument resolves to a managed path, naming the shell
command to use. One shared function, called from each place above.
Lock 3, redirection and save: the file opening checks managed first.
Lock 4, build guard: the scan of step 5 covers these crates with an
allow list of path and count made once from this classified list.
Only Shape adds to it afterwards.
Lock 5, read-only bits. TESTED 2026-11-20 as user shape, uid 10349,
no real root: in a 555 dir a 444 file denied append, mv and rm, so
the lock works here. READ ROOT-WARNING.md in the ecosystem root
first: with real root (uid 0) read-only bits stop nothing, silently.
The server checks at start: uid is not 0, and a test file in a 555
dir denies append, mv and rm. If not, it says NOT LOCKED loudly and
locks 1 to 4 stay in force. Step 10 repeats this test.
If it holds: managed files and dirs are
read-only, the server flips the bit only inside one operation, and
the editor must send its save to the server only: hot-path.rs
writes the file itself at line 195 before notify_server at 205, and
lines 455, 468, 503 write other files. A deliberate chmod still
works. Git by hand then needs a chmod first.
Limit without lock 5: a program started from the shell (editor,
script, python) can still write any file. The git facts watcher of
the server reports those. Done only when the proof of step 10
passes for each builtin, each blocked external name, redirection
and save.
Planned.
